        <item>
            <title>Version 1.0.6</title>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h2>Live Lock Screen Wallpapers</h2>
                <p>Your own videos now play on the macOS Lock Screen. WallX adds its own collection to System Settings &rarr; Wallpaper — pick a video there and it becomes your real lock-screen wallpaper, behind the password field, surviving reboots, with no Aerial replacement needed.</p>
                <h3>Set it up</h3>
                <ol>
                    <li>Play a video in WallX, then click <strong>Add to Lock Screen</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Open <strong>System Settings &rarr; Wallpaper</strong> and choose it under <strong>WallX</strong>.</li>
                    <li>Lock your screen.</li>
                </ol>
                <h3>Also in this release</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Reload Lock Screen</strong> — one tap re-applies your wallpaper if macOS is slow to refresh it.</li>
                    <li>Streamlined the lock-screen tools around the new system-integrated engine.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
